  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kitui Integrated Food Security Project (KIFSP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the Kitui Integrated Food Security Project (KIFSP) is to improve security and resilience to climate shocks for target communities in Kitui County, Kenya.

The project specifically aims to achieve:

1. Improved capacity of local community to manage and protect natural resources sustainably through preparedness and mitigation against the effects of natural calamities.

2. Improved crop production and livestock management characterized by quality and quantity production, preservation.

3. Target beneficiaries in Migwani Ward have increased access to potable water for domestic and agricultural uses and are practising safe hygiene and sanitation practices. 

4. Target communities in Migwani and Yatta/Kwa Vonza Wards are actively engaging the government systems for improved service delivery.</narrative>
  </description>
